@startuml Pattern State sequential
title Device Anomaly Detection & State Transition Sequence
autonumber

actor "Simulation Loop" as Sim
participant "Device" as Dev
participant "ActiveState" as State
participant "IoTSensor" as Sensor
participant "HysteresisCheck\n(Strategy)" as Strat
participant "EventBus" as Bus

' 1. Simulation Tick
Sim -> Dev: handleTick()
activate Dev

' 2. Delegation to State (State Pattern)
Dev -> State: onTick(this)
activate State
note right of State
  ActiveState controls behavior:
  consumes energy, updates sensors
end note

' 3. Trigger Sensor Update
State -> Dev: updateSensors()
activate Dev

loop For each IoTSensor
    ' 4. Physical Measurement
    Dev -> Sensor: measure(baseValue)
    activate Sensor
    Sensor --> Dev: currentValue (simulation noise added)
    deactivate Sensor

    ' 5. Check for Anomaly
    Dev -> Dev: checkAnomaly(sensor, target)
    activate Dev #DarkSalmon

    ' 6. Validation Strategy (Strategy Pattern)
    ' The Device delegates the decision logic to the Strategy
    Dev -> Strat: isAnomaly(current, target, isAlertActive)
    activate Strat
    
    note right of Strat
      Hysteresis Logic:
      Checks if value > threshold
      considering the reset buffer
    end note

    Strat --> Dev: return **true** (Anomaly Confirmed)
    deactivate Strat

    ' 7. Reaction to Failure
    opt Anomaly Detected
        Dev -> Sensor: setAlertActive(true)

        ' A. Notify System (Observer Pattern)
        Dev -> Bus: publish(DEVICE_BREAKDOWN)
        note right: EventLogger & MaintenanceRole\nwill receive this event

        ' B. State Transition (State Pattern)
        create participant "BrokenState" as Broken
        Dev -> Broken: <<create>>
        Dev -> Dev: setState(new BrokenState())
        
        note right of Dev
           CRITICAL: Device stops operating.
           Future ticks will be handled by BrokenState.
        end note
    end

    deactivate Dev
end

deactivate Dev
deactivate State
deactivate Dev
@enduml